  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For a lot of worlds i make i create my own video panel materials/shaders as i like to integrate the streams into world props. However i noticed that the render texture that gets provided through the \"VRC_VideoScreen\" script has flipped uv's and has the texture type set to clamped.\nThe standard videopanel shader uses \"IN.uv_MainTex\" to \"fix\" the flipped nature of the texture, however when integrating the texture in other materials, like the standard unity PBR material (or any custom made shaders in amplify) it will not be able to read from this input, resulting in a flipped texture. \nUse cases for this are:\nIntegrating the video stream in in-world PBR shaded objects like laptop screens or LED walls etc.\n\nExample of how the texture gets displayed when on a object that repeats a texture twice in UV space (0-2 uv)",
